 "notes": "Tetragonal MgSiO3 majorite consolidated from the duplicate Dioptas/JCPDS majorite and mgsio3-maj entries. The richer mgsio3-maj diffraction list is retained. The full I41/a structure, including partial Mg-Si octahedral disorder, is from Angel et al., American Mineralogist 74, 509-512 (1989), COD 9010029. The published coordinates were shifted by +1/2 along x to restore the standard I41/a origin specified in the paper's Table 2 note. Their conventional cell contains eight Mg4Si4O12 garnet units, equivalent to 32 MgSiO3 units; this corrects the earlier Z=16 metadata. Source file(s): JCPDS/current user/jcpds/mgsio3-maj.jcpds, JCPDS/dac_user_jcpds/mgsio3-maj.jcpds, JCPDS/current user/jcpds/ver3/majorite.jcpds.",
